  tutorialId: 0
  titleText: Walls and Undo
  actions:
  - ActionType: 1
    AnimationDirection: 1
    MessageText: So you know how to move the squirell and score a goal! Good, but
      it is not always gonna be so easy.
    MessageDisplayTime: 3
    ActionImage: {fileID: 0}
    ExecuteWithMessage: 0
    ImageActionType: 0
    ActionImageDisplayTime: 0
  - ActionType: 1
    AnimationDirection: 0
    MessageText: Squirell can push the nuts in front of itself. In open field you
      can easily push the nut where you want.
    MessageDisplayTime: 3
    ActionImage: {fileID: 0}
    ExecuteWithMessage: 0
    ImageActionType: 0
    ActionImageDisplayTime: 0
  - ActionType: 1
    AnimationDirection: 3
    MessageText: 'But what about walls?  You can''t move through them and you can"t
      push nuts through them also! '
    MessageDisplayTime: 3
    ActionImage: {fileID: 0}
    ExecuteWithMessage: 0
    ImageActionType: 0
    ActionImageDisplayTime: 0
  - ActionType: 0
    AnimationDirection: 1
    MessageText: 
    MessageDisplayTime: 3
    ActionImage: {fileID: 0}
    ExecuteWithMessage: 0
    ImageActionType: 0
    ActionImageDisplayTime: 0
  - ActionType: 0
    AnimationDirection: 1
    MessageText: 
    MessageDisplayTime: 3
    ActionImage: {fileID: 0}
    ExecuteWithMessage: 0
    ImageActionType: 0
    ActionImageDisplayTime: 0
  - ActionType: 1
    AnimationDirection: 1
    MessageText: See? No way you can push it through a tree wall. No matter how small
      you are, you have no chance!
    MessageDisplayTime: 3
    ActionImage: {fileID: 0}
    ExecuteWithMessage: 0
    ImageActionType: 0
    ActionImageDisplayTime: 0
  - ActionType: 1
    AnimationDirection: 3
    MessageText: To get the nut to the goal you have to push it around the wall.
      Lets move the nut up cause it is  closer way to the goal.
    MessageDisplayTime: 3
    ActionImage: {fileID: 0}
    ExecuteWithMessage: 0
    ImageActionType: 0
    ActionImageDisplayTime: 0
  - ActionType: 0
    AnimationDirection: 2
    MessageText: 
    MessageDisplayTime: 3
    ActionImage: {fileID: 0}
    ExecuteWithMessage: 0
